    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows negative sentiment (e.g., -0.25 or 0.00 in early periods) as it often signals downward pressure.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% when recent history shows mean reversion toward lower prices (e.g., after peaks or sharp spikes).",
    "Apply a lag correction: if true outcome is significantly lower than forecast, reduce next forecast by 5-15% to account for delayed market reaction.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent low prices when sentiment is neutral or positive (e.g., 0.00) to avoid underestimating rebound potential.",
    "Cap forecast spikes above 10% above recent 7-day high to prevent overreaction to short-term volatility.",
    "When sentiment shifts from negative to neutral/positive, apply a gradual upward correction (e.g., +3-5% per day) to align with sentiment momentum."
